              "description": "Identifies xcomm ctl xfer send and recv with zmodem, ymodem or xmodem. Matches the subcommand word anywhere in an xcomm ctl invocation before `--`, because the device name (or --pane) comes between ctl and the subcommand and the word can follow options. Two limits follow. A subcommand after `--` (xcomm ctl -- ttyUSB1 send ls) is not seen, so it keeps only the unknown-executable review floor and a disabled permission does not block it. A matching word elsewhere in the line counts as the subcommand: option text or a wait pattern (--fail-on set, wait run), the text of a send or run (send set), or xfer's direction (xfer send also hits device input). A disabled permission then also blocks that command; this fails closed. dtr, rts, xfer and capture also need the word xcomm requires after them (on/off/toggle/pulse, send/recv, start/stop), so a status field such as status capture does not match.",
              "matcher": {
                "config": {},
